  "verbalization": "Gamma-Glutamylhistidine appears to interact with DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that gamma-Glutamylhistidine acts as a target for G-protein coupled estrogen receptor 1, which in turn is targeted by Fasinumab and another compound, 3,5-Dihydroxy-2-(3-hydroxy-2-methoxyphenyl)-7-methoxychromen-4-one. Both of these compounds are linked to DNA polymerase iota. This implies that gamma-Glutamylhistidine may influence DNA polymerase iota through its interaction with these receptors, potentially modulating the activity of DNA polymerase iota via receptor-mediated signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for gamma-Glutamylhistidine in regulating DNA polymerase iota activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
